# .tagconn

This directory was created by [tagconn](https://github.com/ilomon10/tagconn), a local tool that
shows Claude Code sessions as characters in a 2D office. You opted in to this at install time
(`pnpm office:install`), and it was written once, automatically, by the tagconn hook the first time
you opened this repo with Claude Code.

**It holds no secrets and no host-specific paths.** It is safe to commit.

## What's in here

- `README.md` (this file).
- `office.json` (optional): a portable "office profile" for this project - the floor's name and
  visual style, its room layout, and any named heroes (by role, not by any host-specific data). It
  is only ever written by an explicit "Save office profile" action in the tagconn UI, or by the
  `/tagconn-save` skill - never automatically.

## Restore

If someone else clones this repo and runs tagconn with attribution import on (the default), tagconn
offers to recreate this floor - its name, style, layout and heroes - from `office.json`. Nothing is
ever applied without asking first.

## Save

To capture (or update) the current floor as `office.json`, use tagconn's "Save office profile to
project" action, or run the `/tagconn-save` skill from a Claude Code session in this repo.

## Opt out

If you'd rather tagconn stop touching this repo, delete this directory and replace it with an empty
**file** (not a directory) named `.tagconn`:

```sh
rm -rf .tagconn && touch .tagconn
```

The hook always skips a repo where `.tagconn` already exists in any form (file, directory or
symlink), so this permanently opts the repo out.
